 "audio": "soundtrack.mp3",
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "at": 0.0,
   "real": 0.35,
   "speech": 4.616,
   "len": 4.85,
   "head": 0.234,
   "file": "hook.mp3",
   "file_start": 0.116,
   "hash": "6f4f709bc00e",
   "text": "Someone copies your AI model. How do you prove it was yours?",
   "source": "Sec. I"
  },
  {
   "id": "copy",
   "at": 5.0,
   "real": 5.366,
   "speech": 6.982,
   "len": 7.2,
   "head": 0.218,
   "file": "copy.mp3",
   "file_start": 5.148,
   "hash": "78d8ef3e347e",
   "text": "A trained model is just a file of numbers. The copy is identical, and nothing in it says who did the work.",
   "source": "Sec. I"
  },
  {
   "id": "walk",
   "at": 13.0,
   "real": 13.366,
   "speech": 7.0,
   "len": 7.22,
   "head": 0.22,
   "file": "walk.mp3",
   "file_start": 13.146,
   "hash": "f9fb64ebc26a",
   "text": "But the work leaves a trail. Training is a long walk downhill, every step making the model a little less wrong.",
   "source": "Sec. III-B (SGD on a loss)"
  },
  {
   "id": "receipts",
   "at": 21.5,
   "real": 21.866,
   "speech": 10.085,
   "len": 10.3,
   "head": 0.215,
   "file": "receipts.mp3",
   "file_start": 21.651,
   "hash": "f129a303e60b",
   "text": "Proof-of-Learning keeps that trail: snapshots of the model, with the data and settings behind every step. A verifier replays the biggest steps and checks where they land.",
   "source": "Sec. II-A, IV, Alg. 1 and 2 (the log holds checkpoints, batch indices and hashes, hyperparameters; Top-Q replays the largest updates)"
  },
  {
   "id": "forged",
   "at": 30.5,
   "real": 32.351,
   "speech": 9.227,
   "len": 9.46,
   "head": 0.233,
   "file": "forged.mp3",
   "file_start": 32.118,
   "hash": "f5625d208fec",
   "text": "There's a catch. No computer repeats a long calculation exactly, so the check has to accept close enough. And close enough can be faked.",
   "source": "Sec. II-A, VII-B"
  },
  {
   "id": "lock",
   "at": 40.5,
   "real": 42.351,
   "speech": 9.245,
   "len": 9.46,
   "head": 0.215,
   "file": "lock.mp3",
   "file_start": 42.136,
   "hash": "19bf8c1aa1f8",
   "text": "Our work, SecurePoL, closes that gap with a secret. While the model trains, it also learns planted answers to questions only its owner knows.",
   "source": "Sec. III-A, III-B.3"
  },
  {
   "id": "trap",
   "at": 50.5,
   "real": 52.351,
   "speech": 6.071,
   "len": 6.29,
   "head": 0.219,
   "file": "trap.mp3",
   "file_start": 52.132,
   "hash": "8de1dc5d5f1e",
   "text": "Mapmakers used the same trick: a street that doesn't exist, hidden in the map to catch anyone who copies it.",
   "source": "the analogy is ours"
  },
  {
   "id": "both",
   "at": 58.5,
   "real": 60.351,
   "speech": 4.963,
   "len": 5.18,
   "head": 0.217,
   "file": "both.mp3",
   "file_start": 60.134,
   "hash": "f0df166c43a3",
   "text": "Now a claim needs both: a trail that replays, and a model that knows the secret.",
   "source": "Alg. 2, Sec. VI-I"
  },
  {
   "id": "thief",
   "at": 65.0,
   "real": 66.851,
   "speech": 7.278,
   "len": 7.49,
   "head": 0.212,
   "file": "thief.mp3",
   "file_start": 66.639,
   "hash": "8df4cc3ad1c0",
   "text": "A thief can't name the questions. And scrubbing the secret out changes the model, so it stops matching its own trail.",
   "source": "Sec. III-B.3, II-C.1"
  },
  {
   "id": "scrub",
   "at": 73.5,
   "real": 75.351,
   "speech": 4.889,
   "len": 5.11,
   "head": 0.221,
   "file": "scrub.mp3",
   "file_start": 75.13,
   "hash": "5f19b9aebc47",
   "text": "In our tests, hiding that took real training: the very work they tried to skip.",
   "source": "Sec. III-C.5"
  },
  {
   "id": "cost",
   "at": 79.0,
   "real": 80.851,
   "speech": 7.704,
   "len": 7.92,
   "head": 0.216,
   "file": "cost.mp3",
   "file_start": 80.635,
   "hash": "86a07fed6c50",
   "text": "And the price is small. In our experiments the model stayed almost exactly as accurate, and training took only a little longer.",
   "source": "Sec. VI-B, VI-F"
  },
  {
   "id": "use",
   "at": 87.5,
   "real": 89.351,
   "speech": 3.081,
   "len": 3.31,
   "head": 0.229,
   "file": "use.mp3",
   "file_start": 89.122,
   "hash": "105830dfbc47",
   "text": "This matters wherever a model changes hands.",
   "source": "Sec. V-A"
  },
  {
   "id": "hosp",
   "at": 90.8,
   "real": 92.832,
   "speech": 3.625,
   "len": 3.84,
   "head": 0.215,
   "file": "hosp.mp3",
   "file_start": 92.617,
   "hash": "a0ab09b3009b",
   "text": "A hospital can confirm its model is the one that was audited.",
   "source": "Sec. V-A.1"
  },
  {
   "id": "car",
   "at": 95.0,
   "real": 97.032,
   "speech": 3.863,
   "len": 4.08,
   "head": 0.217,
   "file": "car.mp3",
   "file_start": 96.815,
   "hash": "ab7416a84770",
   "text": "A carmaker can replay a supplier's training after an incident.",
   "source": "Sec. V-A.2"
  },
  {
   "id": "cloud",
   "at": 99.2,
   "real": 101.295,
   "speech": 3.933,
   "len": 4.15,
   "head": 0.217,
   "file": "cloud.mp3",
   "file_start": 101.078,
   "hash": "d5460454dd7a",
   "text": "An AI provider can show that a model was trained on licensed data.",
   "source": "Sec. V-A.3"
  },
  {
   "id": "close",
   "at": 104.0,
   "real": 106.095,
   "speech": 7.773,
   "len": 7.99,
   "head": 0.217,
   "file": "close.mp3",
   "file_start": 105.878,
   "hash": "5c3a06ff5eae",
   "text": "AI models are becoming things we buy, deploy and trust. Where a model came from will matter as much as what it can do.",
   "source": "the authors' view"
  },
  {
